  217                                   ; get_gamma: interlaced Elias gamma in d1.w; d4.w is the 0/1 length seed.
  218                                   ; Gammas are odd-length and each is followed by one flag bit, so a gamma always
  219                                   ; starts at an even position and the queue - which empties every 16 bits, also
  220                                   ; even - can only run out on a continuation bit. Data and transition reads need
  221                                   ; no refill check; 16 is even like 8, so the word queue inherits the argument.
